{
  "about": "Parts of the players' characters, in a 100-unit square, and how they move. A character is [body, color, eyes, mouth, extra], indexes into these lists. A layer is filled (fill) or stroked with round caps (stroke, width); 'body' is the character's color, 'ink' and 'white' the palette's. Eyes, mouths and faces are drawn for a face at y = 50 and move to the body's face; an extra or effect is drawn around (50, 0) at its anchor (the body's top or chin, or the face), an extra behind the body when it says so. Motion: at time t (seconds) a character breathes, scaling its whole drawing about (50, base) by sy = 1 + a, sx = 1 - a / 2 with a = idle.breathe.amount * sin(2 pi t / idle.breathe.period). Eyes whose part allows it blink: with h the FNV-1a hash of the nickname's UTF-8 bytes, period P = every[0] + (every[1] - every[0]) * (h & 0xffff) / 65535 and offset o = P * ((h >> 16) & 0xffff) / 65535; while x = (t + o) mod P is under duration the eyes scale vertically about (50, face) by 1 - 0.9 * sin(pi * x / duration). An expression started at time s shows, while t - s < hold (or always when looped), its eyes and mouth from faces (or eyes and mouths) by name, instead of the character's, except eyes marked keep; its effects; and its motion at progress p = min((t - s) / duration, 1), or ((t - s) mod duration) / duration when looped. A motion's keys are [p, dx, dy, sx, sy, rot]; between two keys each value is interpolated with smoothstep on the segment's fraction (linear when ease is linear), and the transform is translate(pivot + (dx, dy)) rotate(rot degrees) scale(sx, sy) translate(-pivot), with the pivot (50, base) for the body and the effect's pivot for an effect. The body's motion applies to the whole drawing after breathing; an effect's loops with t - s on top of it.",
